  "observations": [
    "Concurrent writes on different people conflict: at 1,006 people, 8 of 10 and 47 of 50 simultaneous visit starts were rejected with 409.",
    "At 50 req/s (30% writes) throughput fell to 5.6-5.9 req/s; at 5,006 people 568 of 750 requests timed out after 120 s.",
    "Every workspace read returns the whole permitted organisation: 0.8 MB at 1,006 people, 77 MB at 100,006 people.",
    "A single write grows faster than linearly: 138 ms at 1,006 people, 3.7 s at 20,006, 20.8 s at 50,006 and 80.9 s at 100,006.",
    "After the 5,000-person sustained phase the local database stayed locked and further seeding hung; the 20,000+ sizes were therefore measured in a separate read-only run."
